        "notes": [
          {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "A flaw was found in PostgreSQL. This buffer over-read vulnerability in the `pg_restore_attribute_stats()` function allows a table maintainer to infer memory values. By providing array values of unmatched length, a malicious table maintainer can cause query planning to read past the end of an array, leading to information disclosure.",
